[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AttributionEntry" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://attribution/attribution_entry.gd" id="1_entry"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_entry")
id = "quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack"
creator = "Quaternius"
source_name = "Ultimate Nature Pack"
source_version = "June 2019"
creator_url = "https://quaternius.com"
source_url = "https://quaternius.com"
support_url = "https://www.patreon.com/quaternius"
license_name = "CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication"
license_url = "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
license_file = "res://assets/licenses/Quaternius_UltimateAnimatedAnimals_License.txt"
attribution_required = false
required_notice = ""
conditions = ""
assets_used = PackedStringArray("WoodLog_Moss", "Rock_Moss_3", "Bush_1", "Rock_1", "BirchTree_1", "BushBerries_1", "Rock_Moss_2", "Rock_Moss_5", "Lilypad", "Cactus_1", "PalmTree_1", "BirchTree_Snow_3", "Bush_Snow_1")
per_file_licensing = false
notes = "CC0 — crediting is courtesy, not compliance. Pack ships its own License.txt at
`source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature Pack - Jun 2019.../License.txt`, byte-identical boilerplate
to the one already preserved as license_file for the Ultimate Animated Animal Pack (same
generic Quaternius CC0 1.0 dedication text, not pack-specific) — reused rather than
duplicated, same reasoning as quaternius_poly_pizza_characters.tres.

First use of this pack: three pieces (WoodLog_Moss, Rock_Moss_3, Bush_1) composed into the
Den move-in prop (project/assets/props/den/Den.tscn) — see gdd.md's Level & world design
for what a move-in prop is.

Second use: Rock_1 (plain, non-moss) as the Rock terrain tile's model
(project/assets/terrain/rock_1/Rock1.tscn) — the load-bearing `cover`/`rocks` source for
Fox/Rabbit habitat (terrain.md). Deliberately a different piece from the Den's Rock_Moss_3:
the Den is decoration, this is a paintable terrain tile, and the plain Rock reads more
generic/repeatable than a mossy one for something the player places many of.

Third use (2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 5): BirchTree_1.fbx and BushBerries_1.fbx
newly imported as project/assets/terrain/birch_tree/BirchTree.tscn and
project/assets/terrain/bush_berries/BushBerries.tscn, both wired as new Forest
model_scenes entries (see project/data/terrain/forest.tres's header). Bush_1.fbx (already
listed above from the Den prop use) is ALSO now reused a second time as
project/assets/terrain/bush/Bush.tscn, another new Forest model_scenes entry — same source
file, no new assets_used entry needed since the filename is already recorded.

Fourth use (2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 6): Rock_Moss_2.fbx and Rock_Moss_5.fbx
newly imported as project/assets/terrain/rock_moss_2/Rock_Moss_2.fbx and
project/assets/terrain/rock_moss_5/Rock_Moss_5.fbx, both composed (never referenced
directly) into 2 new Rock model_scenes entries — RockCluster5.tscn and RockCluster6.tscn
(see project/data/terrain/rock.tres's header). Deliberately different Rock_Moss_N files
from Rock_Moss_3 (already used by RockCluster1.tscn and the Den prop, both listed above)
so this pass adds genuinely new pieces rather than a third use of the same file; the pack
ships 7 Rock_Moss_N.fbx variants total (Rock_Moss_1..7, confirmed on disk), of which only
3, 2, and 5 are used anywhere in the project as of this pass.

Fifth use (2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 8): Lilypad.fbx newly imported as
res://assets/terrain/lilypad/Lilypad.fbx (one raw copy, shared by uid reference — same
Rock_Moss_5/Rock_Moss_2 convention above), composed into 2 new Water model_scenes entries:
project/assets/terrain/water_lilypad_1/WaterLilypad1.tscn (2 lilypad instances) and
project/assets/terrain/water_lilypad_2/WaterLilypad2.tscn (4 lilypad instances), both
siblings that instance the existing project/assets/terrain/water/Water.tscn as a base (see
project/data/terrain/water.tres's own header). The task brief that spawned this work
originally named project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres as the file
to modify, written before the on-disk `find` confirmed Lilypad.fbx actually lives in THIS
pack (Ultimate Nature Pack), not among the standalone poly.pizza downloads that other file
tracks — recorded here instead, the correct source file for where the asset was actually
found.

Sixth use (2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 9): Cactus_1.fbx and PalmTree_1.fbx newly
imported as res://assets/terrain/wild_grass_cactus/WildGrassCactus.tscn and
res://assets/terrain/wild_grass_palm/WildGrassPalm.tscn, initially wired as 2 of 3 new Wild
grass model_scenes entries (see project/data/terrain/wild_grass.tres's own header) that
instance the existing res://assets/terrain/wild_grass/WildGrass.tscn as a base plus one
desert-flavor prop each — same "instance the existing scene, add a prop" pattern the
Fifth use (WaterLilypad1/2.tscn) already established. Cactus_1.fbx was directly confirmed
in this pack at plan time; PalmTree_1.fbx was flagged unconfirmed at plan time and
confirmed by this task's own on-disk `find` (a same-named PalmTree_1.fbx also exists in
the separate Nature Crops Pack's growth-stage series — this is the Ultimate Nature Pack's
standalone tree, a different file).

REVERTED FROM THE RANDOM POOL THE SAME DAY (human eyeball pass): wild_grass.tres's human
ruling was that plain Wild grass must stay the default, not one-of-N-equal-weight — Cactus
and Palm were pulled from `model_scenes` back down to the single original entry, and are
kept imported here on disk (not deleted) for sub-project B's player-facing style picker to
wire in later. The 3rd variant this pass tried, a Coconut prop sourced from the Nature
Crops Pack, was rejected outright ("does not look good at all") and fully deleted rather
than deferred — see quaternius_nature_crops_pack.tres for that one's removal note.

Seventh use (2026-09-04, habitat-tiers Task 8): BirchTree_Snow_3.fbx and Bush_Snow_1.fbx
newly imported as res://assets/terrain/birch_tree_snow/BirchTree_Snow_3.fbx and
res://assets/terrain/bush_snow/Bush_Snow_1.fbx, composed into the new Snowfield terrain's
sole model_scenes entry (project/assets/terrain/snowfield/Snowfield.tscn — see that
scene's own header for sourcing/scale detail; project/data/terrain/snowfield.tres emits
the new `snow` habitat tag). Both pieces are the pack's dedicated snow-season variants of
trees/bushes already used elsewhere in this file (BirchTree_1, Bush_1) — a deliberate
different-season pick, not a duplicate import of the same file.

The pack ships many more trees/rocks/grass pieces beyond these thirteen; append to
assets_used as each is imported, do NOT create a second entry for this pack (same
convention as quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres)."
